    "issue_alignment": "The striped-header decoder reads the stripe-count byte N immediately after consuming the last metadata byte (the ulen varint) without verifying that a byte remains. The PoC is a CRAM 3.0 file whose SAM-header block (method RANS_PR0 = 5, comp_size = 2) contains the 2-byte payload 0x08 0x00: byte 0 sets X_STRIPE and byte 1 is the single-byte ulen varint that consumes the last metadata byte, so c_meta_len reaches in_size and in[2] performs a one-byte read past the end of the compressed block, a heap-buffer-overflow."
